SUMMARY:Bent Creek Hike!! 
DESCRIPTION:WNC Sierra Club\n**Join us for an early morning walk in Bent C
 reek and lunch at the Bent Creek Bistro on Tuesday November 10\, 2026. We 
 will be meeting in West Asheville at 8:30 am.**\n\n**This will be a two pa
 rt hike:**\n1. **LOOP ONE:** We will hike about ¼ mile from Hardtimes Tra
 ilhead to Old Bent Creek Gap Road\, turn right\, and do a \\~ 2 mile loop 
 that takes us along Bent Creek to Lake Powhatan\, around the lake\, then a
 long the Pine Tree loop where we will take a shortcut to the other side of
  the loop and return on the other side of the lake. There will be wonderfu
 l views of the stream\, lake\, and woods!\n2. **LOOP TWO**: When we arrive
  back at the turn to Hardtimes Trailhead\, you can head up to your car **O
 R** do a second loop from there (this one is also about 2 miles). We will 
 go along Bent Creek Gap Road to Cedar Mountain/Carolina Mountain trail loo
 p and then back on the Creekside Trail (next to Bent Creek) to the Hard Ti
 mes parking lot. In the middle of this loop\, we will be at the Arboretum 
 and have a chance to look around as well as have an early lunch at the [Be
 nt Creek Bistro](https://www.ncarboretum.org/plan-a-visit/dining/).. Both 
 loops are well maintained and gentle with maybe a total of 200 feet elevat
 ion gain.\n· **LUNCH**\\- In the middle of the 2nd loop\\\, we will be at
  the Arboretum and have a chance to look around as well as have lunch at t
 he [Bent Creek Bistro](https://www.ncarboretum.org/plan-a-visit/dining/). 
 If you prefer to bring lunch that’s fine!\n· **If you do both loops**\n
 o your total hike will be \\~ 5 miles and include lunch and exploring the 
 Arboretum a bit…\no my guess is we will be back at the parking area arou
 nd 2:30…\nPlease plan to bring rain gear regardless of the forecast\, sn
 acks and water\, and *your own lunch if you don’t want to buy lunch at t
 he Bistro*.\n--> No dogs on this hike please\n**To register for this hike 
 and/or to ask questions please do the following two things:**\n\n1. Go to 
 the Sierra Club [Campfire](https://act.sierraclub.org/events/details?formc
 ampaignid=701Po00002IyMTlIAN&addattendee=true) website and sign up.\n\nEma
 il or text Ed Maggart - [edmaggart@gmail.com](mailto:edmaggart@gmail.com) 
 - 828-713-0541 to get any questions answered about the trip and find out a
 bout meeting locations and the possibility of carpooling
